# docs/DETERMINISM.md is append-only with hand-numbered `## N.` sections:
# every edit is a whole new tail written after the last one, never a change
# to existing text. `merge=appendonly` names a driver that keeps the common
# base and concatenates both sides' new tail — the correct 3-way answer for a
# file with that shape, not a keep-both hack. The driver itself lives at
# `ci/merge-appendonly.py` and is registered locally (git attributes cannot
# carry a driver command) by `ci/setup-merge-drivers.sh`, called from
# `ci/t0.sh`. See that script and the driver's own header for the rest.
#
# docs/WORKLIST.md must never carry `merge=union` OR `merge=appendonly`, and
# the reason is unchanged: it is self-evolving — the three `## NOW` blocks are
# edited in place, not appended to — and a union on a file like that is
# precisely the defect that produced a stale figure surviving as a duplicate
# block. That damage is still legible in the file: the COLD START INDEX today
# holds `ci-unfalsifiable-root` twice, with "10 of 84" in one row and "4 of 84"
# in the other, because a branch replaced its own row and a union kept both.
#
# What it carries instead, since 2026-08-16, is `merge=docregions` — a driver
# that resolves an add/add hunk ONLY inside a region the file itself declares
# with `MERGE-REGION BEGIN/END` markers, and only when neither side touched
# existing text. WORKLIST declares exactly one such region, around the COLD
# START INDEX table body, which is where 36 of the last 40 commits to the file
# landed. All three `## NOW` blocks are outside it and merge exactly as they
# did before, conflicting when they genuinely disagree.
#
# docs/PARITY-ROADMAP.md and ci/figures.toml are the same shape with the
# region at the tail: every branch appends a new `## N.` section, or a new
# `[[figure]]`, at EOF. They were the next two most common collisions —
# measured 2026-08-16 over 48 unmerged branches, 26 of which would not rebase
# onto main: WORKLIST 13, PARITY-ROADMAP 11, figures.toml 4.
#
# docs/DETERMINISM.md stays on `appendonly`. It is the one file where EVERY
# edit really is a whole new tail, that driver's byte-prefix refusal is the
# strictest thing available, and it is proven; there is no measured collision
# there to justify moving it to a more general driver.
#
# ci/checks/gameplay-falsifiable.toml and ci/checks/gameplay-baseline.toml are
# the same shape again, measured 2026-08-17 as the new top collision once the
# three above stopped being one: gameplay-falsifiable.toml conflicted on 4 of
# that day's gameplay branches and gameplay-baseline.toml on 2, both for the
# same reason — every branch appends rows at the tail. gameplay-falsifiable.toml
# gets `to-eof check=toml-scenarios`, no key: its rows are multi-line
# `[[scenario]]` stanzas, and a real re-sweep of an EXISTING scenario still
# conflicts by line exactly as before, which is correct — only a clean new
# stanza reaches the append rule. gameplay-baseline.toml gets
# `key=toml-key check=unique-toml-key`: its rows are one `key = "verdict"`
# assignment per line, the same shape WORKLIST's index table is, just without
# the Markdown.
#
# ci/t0.sh is measured 2026-08-17 as the single biggest source of merge
# contention in the queue: six branches touched it that day with zero
# deletions between them, each adding a new check block next to the existing
# one it is topically closest to rather than at a shared tail. Its region is
# therefore the whole executable body — `checks`, BEGIN right after `cd`, END
# right before the closing sentinel — not one table or a `to-eof` tail, and it
# carries `check=bash-syntax` rather than a key: a check block is not named
# anywhere the merge can read, so the one thing left to verify unconditionally
# is that the result still parses. This is executable code, so a wrong merge
# breaks the gate for every branch, not just its author's; see
# `ci/merge-docregions.py`'s own header for why the width of the region does
# not weaken what it refuses. `ci/t1.sh` was checked the same day and is NOT
# this shape — real edits, not appends, on a fixed two-call sequence whose
# order is load-bearing — so it carries no attribute here.
#
# Both drivers are registered per checkout by `ci/setup-merge-drivers.sh` —
# git attributes cannot carry a driver command — which `ci/t0.sh`,
# `ci/t0-remote.sh` and `ci/lanes.sh` all call. See those scripts and each
# driver's own header for the rest.
docs/DETERMINISM.md merge=appendonly
docs/WORKLIST.md merge=docregions
docs/PARITY-ROADMAP.md merge=docregions
ci/figures.toml merge=docregions
ci/checks/gameplay-falsifiable.toml merge=docregions
ci/checks/gameplay-baseline.toml merge=docregions
ci/t0.sh merge=docregions
# Added 2026-09-05 with the survival corpus, by KIND and not by the measured
# ranking below — that ranking is over files that existed on 2026-08-18 and
# this one did not. It is the same shape as gameplay-falsifiable.toml in the
# only respect the driver cares about: `ci/corpus-falsifiable.py --sweep`
# rewrites the WHOLE document, so without a region marker a re-swept ledger
# gets the driver's refusals and none of its resolutions, and several lanes
# append survival scenarios to one tail. The seventh-driver bar below is about
# spending a day ranking candidates; it is not an argument for shipping a
# second ledger of a driven kind undriven.
ci/checks/survival-falsifiable.toml merge=docregions
docs/FINDINGS.md merge=docregions
ci/checks/test-targets.toml merge=docregions

