# THE COVERAGE IS DONE. Measured 2026-08-18 — do not go looking for a seventh.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every driver above was added because somebody measured what it would free.
# The obvious next question is which file to add next, and it has now been
# answered by exhaustion rather than by guessing, so nobody has to spend a day
# on it again.
#
# THE INSTRUMENT. All 46 queued branches, all 1035 pairs, three-way merged
# against main with `git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only`, and every
# conflicted path recorded. No worktree, no rebase, no gate — about eight
# minutes. NOTE THE ONE TRAP: `git merge-tree` does NOT run custom merge
# drivers, so the files above still report as conflicts under it. They are
# resolved in a real gate and must be subtracted before ranking; a ranking
# that skips that step just rediscovers the drivers already here, which is
# what the first pass of this measurement did.
#
# THE RESULT.
#
#     79 of 1035 pairs conflict at all                     (7.6%)
#     60 of those 79 conflict ONLY in files driven above
#     19 pairs have a conflict in an UNDRIVEN file
#
# and those 19 are spread over 20 different files. The whole undriven ranking:
#
#     5  ci/t2-regiondiff.sh
#     3  ci/checks/gameplay/README.md
#     2  tools/region-differ/src/main.rs
#     2  tools/oracle-runner/src/trace.rs
#     2  ci/vanilla-reach-census.py
#     1  each — sixteen further files, one pair apiece
#
# THE BAR THIS HAS TO CLEAR, AND WHY NOTHING CLEARS IT. The docregions pair
# (gameplay-falsifiable.toml + gameplay-baseline.toml) freed 39 pairs and saved
# six recordings, ~4.0 h. The best remaining candidate frees 5 — an eighth of
# that — and it is not even the right kind of file:
#
#   * `ci/t2-regiondiff.sh` is a 22-line stub on main that four branches each
#     grow independently, to 45, 45, 289 and 292 lines. Two of the four agree
#     (blob 919d48dc); the other two disagree with them and with each other.
#     That is four branches rewriting one young file, not several branches
#     appending to a shared one, and a driver that kept both sides would
#     produce a script that is the concatenation of two different scripts. It
#     is the `## NOW` case exactly: the conflict is visible and the silently
#     merged result would not be.
#   * `ci/checks/gameplay/README.md` frees 3, over 12 commits with 12 distinct
#     hunk starts — scattered edits, no region structure to declare.
#   * everything else frees one pair, which is one rebase somebody does by hand
#     once.
#
# Same verdict, same method and same reasons as `ci/t1.sh` and `docs/BENCH.md`,
# both of which were examined and rejected earlier — and `docs/BENCH.md` shows
# up here at exactly one pair, which corroborates that call from a direction it
# was not made from.
#
# So: the remaining conflict surface is 19 pairs of 1035 spread over 20 files,
# and adding a driver to any of them would be adding machinery, and a marker
# line every future edit has to respect, to buy back a rebase or two. **Reopen
# this only with a fresh sweep showing a single undriven file above ~20 pairs**,
# not because a file feels collision-prone.
#
