# REOPENED ONCE, ON THE TERMS ABOVE — docs/FINDINGS.md, 2026-09-05.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The sweep above was taken 2026-08-18. `docs/FINDINGS.md` was created on
# **2026-08-19**, the day after, so it could not appear in that ranking and its
# absence from it says nothing. It is now by a wide margin the largest
# collision in the queue, and the file's own header is the reason: every lane
# appends one bullet at the tail and nothing else about the file changes, which
# is an add/add hunk at a single anchor between every pair of lanes that
# reports a finding.
#
# THE INSTRUMENT. The 37 branches ahead of main that touch the file, all 666
# pairs, three-way merged on that path alone — `git merge-file` for git's own
# answer and `ci/merge-docregions.py` for the driver's, on inputs carrying the
# marker, which is the state after main has it and both sides have rebased.
# 595 of the 666 have the file in their merge base; the other 71 are an add/add
# of the whole file, which the driver handles from an empty base.
#
#     588 of 595 pairs conflict under git's default three-way   (98.8%)
#      37 of 595 conflict under merge=docregions                 (6.2%)
#     ---
#     551 pairs freed, 93.8% of the collisions on that path
#
# That is 14x the 39 pairs the gameplay-falsifiable/baseline pair freed, and
# 110x the best remaining candidate in the ranking above. It clears the ~20-pair
# bar by 27x. The 37 that remain are real disagreements — two lanes correcting
# the same finding — and must stay conflicts.
#
# It gets `to-eof check=unique-bullet-line`, no key: a finding is a Markdown
# bullet rather than a keyed row, so the post-condition counts the bullets'
# own first lines and refuses a merge that asserts one more often than the side
# asserting it most. `ci/merge-appendonly-falsify.sh` cases 29, 29b, 29c and
# 29d are its proof, and 29b and 29c are the ones that matter: a rewritten
# finding still conflicts, and a lane replacing its own earlier line does not
# get it back beside the replacement. That last is the exact defect `merge=union`
# left legible in WORKLIST.
#
