# AND A SECOND, ON THE SAME TERMS — ci/checks/test-targets.toml, 2026-09-05.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 36 branches ahead of main touch it, and 193 of their 630 pairs conflict on it
# — the second-largest collision in the queue and ~10x the ~20-pair bar. It is
# absent from the 2026-08-18 ranking for a different reason from FINDINGS: it
# existed, and that sweep ranked whole-merge conflicts after subtracting the
# driven files, so a pair conflicting BOTH here and in a driven file was
# counted once, under the driven file. The undriven ranking is a ranking of
# pairs whose ONLY conflict is undriven; it is the right question for "what
# should be driven next" and the wrong one for "what does this file cost".
#
#     193 of 630 pairs conflict under git's default three-way   (30.6%)
#      18 of 630 conflict under merge=docregions                 (2.9%)
#     ---
#     175 pairs freed, 90.7%
#
# Its shape is `ci/t0.sh`'s, not `ci/figures.toml`'s: a branch adding a cargo
# target adds a whole `[[bucket]]` stanza beside the bucket it is topically
# closest to, and `light-engine-2`'s six hunks start at lines 182, 250, 274,
# 287, 628 and 709. So the region is the whole body and `check=toml-buckets`
# carries the weight — the file must parse, `[[bucket]]` ids must be unique,
# and no target may be listed in two buckets, which is the sharper of the two:
# two lanes can add differently-named buckets and still put one target in both,
# and `ci/check-test-targets.py` is entitled to assume a target runs in one
# gate. `ci/merge-appendonly-falsify.sh` cases 30, 30b, 30c, 30d, 30e; 30 puts
# both sides' bucket at a MID-FILE anchor, because an append at the tail would
# be resolved by the tail rule alone and would not exercise the region's width.
#
# The ranking above stands for everything else. These are two files, measured,
# on the terms that paragraph set — not a licence to add a ninth on a feeling,
# and the honest reading of both is that the paragraph's METHOD was right and
# its ranking had a blind spot the method itself explains.
